The present report documents the entire software engineering lifecycle followed and is structured around four major parts:
•  Part One establishes the project framework and organizational context, presenting host company SOUTARAH GROUP, existing system analysis, stated objectives, system specifications, and task planning;
•  Part Two is dedicated to the conceptual study, detailing the UP/UML methodological approach and design models (use case, activity, sequence, and class diagrams);
•  Part Three develops the technical architecture, justifying technology choices (React, React Native, Node.js, MySQL) and explicating the global software infrastructure;
•  Part Four describes the practical implementation of the web platform and mobile application, detailing developed features, validation testing, achieved results, and financial analysis.

198:
At an operational level, the project aims to:
• Develop a modern web portal interactively showcasing all 6 service divisions and product catalog;
• Develop a native mobile application (Android / iOS) dedicated to live vehicle fleet browsing, conflict-free booking with dynamic pricing, and order tracking;
• Implement a hybrid multi-item shopping cart (vehicles and trade supplies) with automated tax calculation (Net, VAT 18%, TDT 2.5%);
• Automate the generation of official 2-page pro-forma PDF quotations (including technical datasheets and visual imagery) ready for printing or digital signature;
• Develop a centralized administrative back-office dashboard to manage quotes, vehicles, client accounts, and system notifications;
• Integrate a transactional email notification system for real-time customer and admin alerts.

