• Complete trading catalog management (product creation, inventory, pricing adjustments);
  • Customer account administration and partner discount tier management.

3. Technical Requirements and Constraints :
  • Security ;
  • High availability and performance ;
  • Cross-platform portability ;

270:
Within the framework of our project, the system incorporates three principal actors:
• The Visitor / Client : browses the product catalog, composes multi-service shopping carts on the Web, executes vehicle reservations on the Mobile application, and downloads official PDF quotes;
• The Administrator : oversees all commercial operations, manages the fleet, updates tariffs, and validates customer quotations;
• The System / REST API : enforces business rules, performs algorithmic conflict-free date verification, and orchestrates notification delivery.

508:
The MySQL database was modeled to guarantee relational integrity across transactions. It comprises the following core entity tables:
• Users & Clients: Credentials (email, Bcrypt hashed password, role 'CLIENT' / 'ADMIN') linked to individual or corporate profiles;
• Vehicles: Brand, model, category, daily rate, availability status, technical specifications, and photographs;
• Reservations: Start/end dates, driver requirement option, destination zone, total amount, and validation status;
• Services & Products: Comprehensive catalog covering all 6 business divisions with itemized specs and tariffs;
• Quotations: Unique reference code (e.g. DMD-2026-XXXX), generation timestamp, Net and Gross totals, and status;
• Notifications: System alerts dispatched to clients and administrative personnel.

